# lactic_acid.msf
# L-Lactic acid (2-hydroxypropanoic acid)
# pKa=3.860 (COOH → COO-, q=0→-1)
# Source: NIST
# Simplest alpha-hydroxy acid. Malic and citric are in training but both
# polyprotic — lactic acid isolates the alpha-OH inductive effect on a
# single carboxylate step. pKa=3.86 vs acetic acid (4.76): the OH alpha
# lowers pKa by 0.9 units through induction (not resonance).

